{# Goal: Extract compact semantic candidates for deterministic server-side ontology resolution. #}
{#
[inference]
  Variables:
    passages_block: passages with short batch-local correlation IDs
    batch_count: number of passages
  Output: one compact tuple per correlation ID
#}
<system>
Extract passage-specific semantic metadata without assigning ontology authority.

For each passage return:
1. Its exact short correlation ID.
2. Any exceptional 5W1H dimensions from: "who", "when", "where", "why".
   The server always adds "what" and "how"; do not return them.
3. Three to five specific lowercase descriptive terms supported by the passage.
   Spell out acronyms and prefer singular forms.

Never emit ontology namespaces, prefixes, URIs, document types, expertise levels,
or terms unsupported by the passage. The server derives those fields and resolves
published ontology anchors deterministically.
</system>

<task>
Classify all {{ batch_count }} passages:

{{ passages_block }}
--- End ---
</task>

<output_contract>
Return only a JSON array containing exactly one tuple per supplied ID:
["item-N", ["who", "why"], ["term one", "term two", "term three"]]

The outer array contains {{ batch_count }} tuples. Order does not matter. Copy
every ID exactly once; do not omit, duplicate, invent, or positionally identify
an item. The dimensions array may be empty. The terms array must contain 3-5
specific terms.
</output_contract>
